 61ZN c  Compiled (evaluated) dataset from 2009An01:                            
 61ZN2c  Phys Rev C 79, 024312 (2009)                                           
 61ZN c  Compiled by S. Geraedts and B. Singh (McMaster); April 9, 2009         
 61ZN c  E=142, 148 MeV beam provided by Argonne National Lab.                  
 61ZN2c  Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g, (particle)|g coin, angular distributions using
 61ZN3c  GAMMASPHERE array of Ge detectors. The charged particles were detected 
 61ZN4c  using Microball array and |DE-E telescopes. Comparisons with cranked   
 61ZN5c  Nilsson-Strutinsky calculations                                        
 61ZN c  Data for levels below 8500 keV are from 2006An31:                      
 61ZN2c  Eur Phys J A 30, 381 (2006).                                           
 61ZN3c  See XUNDL-6 dataset for {+61}Zn, compiled from 2006An31                
 61ZN cG $ R(30|'-83|') is angular asymmetry ratio: expected ratio is |?1.6-1.7 
 61ZN2cG for |DJ=2, quadrupole and |?0.7-0.8 for |DJ=1, dipole transition       
 61ZN cG E(X)$ Doublet structure                                                
 61ZN cL E$From least-squares fit to E|g's (by compilers);                      
 61ZN2cL normalized |h{+2}=1.3. Uncertainty assumed as 1 keV when not stated    
 61ZN cL $ Nomenclature for configuration assignments is [p{-1}p{-2},n{-1}n{-2}]
 61ZN2cL where p{-1} and n{-1} denote number of proton or neutron holes in the  
 61ZN3cL orbitals of high-j 1f{-7/2} shell; p{-2} and n{-2} denote the number of
 61ZN4cL (proton or neutron) particles in the high-j 1g{-9/2} shell, relative to
 61ZN5cL the closed {+56}Ni core. Active orbitals for protons and neutrons are: 
 61ZN6cL 1f{-7/2}, 1g{-9/2}, 1f{-5/2}, 2p{-3/2} and 2p{-1/2}; the number of     
 61ZN7cL particles in the last three orbitals are denoted as p{-3} or n{-3}     
